131	    /**
132	     * Returns the stored E.164 {@code telephone} formatted for humans: the recognized country code
133	     * (with its leading {@code '+'}), a space, then the national digits grouped in threes from the
134	     * left and separated by spaces (for example {@code '+61412345678'} renders as
135	     * {@code '+61 412 345 678'}). The split into country code and national number reuses
136	     * {@link #countryCodeOf(String)}, the single definition of that split. Returns {@code null} when
137	     * the owner has no telephone, and returns the raw E.164 value unchanged when it carries no
138	     * recognized country code. This is the single definition of an owner's human-readable telephone.
139	     *
140	     * @return the human-formatted telephone, or {@code null} when the owner has no telephone
141	     */
